mod:defer_body_may_not_pass;
// A `pass` OR A `return` IN A `defer` BODY IS REFUSED BY NAME (TYPE-040, D-163 rule 7, DEF-417's open half). The body runs at every
// exit of its block, the function's own `pass` among them, so its `pass` re-entered it in the emitter until npkc's stack net fired:
// exit 3, no message, on every landing before this one. `dp_pass_total_in_defer` and `m2_mov_dloop_wendb_L2` reach that road only under
// the pending-exit walk: before it TAINT-001 and MOVE-001 stopped them for another reason. TYPE-040 comes first now.
